  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reporters without borders Sweden (CSO strategy 2025-2029) - Reporters without borders Sweden 2025-2029 (CSO strategy)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Reportrar utan gr&#xe4;nser Sverige (CSO strategin 2025-2029)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reporters Without Borders Sweden (RSF Sweden) has applied for project funding from Sida within the framework of Sweden&#x2019;s strategy for development cooperation with civil society 2025&#x2013;2029, as well as under a targeted call for Ukraine.

The main CSO application concerns the project &#x201c;Strengthened Democracy through Increased Press Freedom&#x201d; and now amounts to SEK 11.9 million for the period 1 December 2025 to 31 December 2028. The project aims to strengthen free and independent journalism through capacity development and organisational support to six local partner organisations in Ukraine, Belarus, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Ecuador, and Colombia. The overall objective is to increase freedom of the press and freedom of expression, protect journalists, and ensure access to reliable information in vulnerable contexts.

In addition, RSF Sweden has submitted a separate application under a targeted Ukraine call. The project &#x201c;Free Media, Strong Democracy: Support to Sustainable Journalism in Ukraine&#x201d; amounts to SEK 2.686 million for the period 1 January 2026 to 31 December 2027. The intervention focuses on protecting press freedom, building the capacity of local and regional media, and strengthening international coordination in a context shaped by war and disinformation.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Reportrar utan gr&#xe4;nser Sverige (RSF Sverige) har ans&#xf6;kt om projektst&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sida inom ramen f&#xf6;r strategin f&#xf6;r Sveriges utvecklingssamarbete med civila samh&#xe4;llet 2025&#x2013;2029 samt en riktad utlysning f&#xf6;r Ukraina. Den ordinarie CSO-ans&#xf6;kan avser projektet &#x201d;St&#xe4;rkt demokrati genom &#xf6;kad pressfrihet&#x201d; och uppg&#xe5;r nu till 11,9 miljoner kronor f&#xf6;r perioden 1 december 2025 &#x2013; 31 december 2028. Projektet syftar till att st&#xe4;rka fri och oberoende journalistik genom kapacitetsutveckling och organisationsst&#xf6;d till sex lokala partnerorganisationer i Ukraina, Belarus, DRK, Ecuador och Colombia. Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att &#xf6;ka press- och yttrandefrihet, skydda journalister och s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla tillg&#xe5;ng till tillf&#xf6;rlitlig information i utsatta kontexter. Ut&#xf6;ver detta har RSF Sverige l&#xe4;mnat in en separat ans&#xf6;kan inom en riktad Ukraina-utlysning. Projektet &#x201d;Fria medier, stark demokrati: St&#xf6;d till h&#xe5;llbar journalistik i Ukraina&#x201d; omfattar 2,686 miljoner kronor f&#xf6;r perioden 1 januari 2026 &#x2013; 31 december 2027. Insatsen fokuserar p&#xe5; skydd av pressfrihet, kapacitetsutveckling av lokala och regionala medier samt internationell samordning, i en kontext pr&#xe4;glad av krig och desinformation.</narrative>
  </description>
